[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The semantics engine is not importable from the repository root

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[WORK]
UID: WORK-SEMANTICS-CLI-MODULE-PATH
TITLE: The semantics engine is not importable from the repository root
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
`python3 -m sdoc_semantics` does not work from the repository root, because
dev/scripts is not on PYTHONPATH. The engine is only reachable through
`scribe semantics` or through the strictdoc-grammar-extract path form, and the
-m spelling fails with an import error that reads like a missing dependency.
Cheapest fix: put dev/scripts on the path the dev shell exports, or retire the
-m form and document the two entry points that do work.
<<<
